The issue desk is built in `/tmp/claude-0/runs/r15/desk9-xstate-haiku-1/src/`: `App.tsx` is the root component, and the XState v5 machines are `deskMachine.ts`, `issuesMachine.ts`, `helpMachine.ts`, `settingsMachine.ts` and `shared.ts`. Server mutations run as spawned callback actors that report back by op id, so optimistic changes can be undone on decline. `./check` passes and all 30 visible tests pass (4 of 15 runs used). I'm unsure about four points: an assign decline shows the raw server message with no prefix, since the brief gives none; changing the help query clears the selected hit, which the brief does not say; the count-after-decline path is not covered by the visible tests (it relies on the same ordering the passing accepted-close test exercises); and the one console 404 is probably the page's favicon, which I did not check.